      next = 4,
      beijing = 3530,
      sentence = [[
"So one day, I went to Italy in the 16th century and told a street musician that his violin was too ugly and crude. That he should wrap the wood in pelts, and carve the body into more graceful curves."

"He did exactly as I said, and the new violin became widely popular. I was very satisfied. But 3 years later, all the violins in Italy reverted back to their original style. Not 300, not 30, but only 3 years."

"I was deeply puzzled. What happened in those 3 years? Was it time's choice, or was someone interfering with it?"
]],
      music = "30_WarmSnow",
      voice = "est_10112_3.mp3"
    },
    [4] = {
      uid = 947,
      next = 5,
      beijing = 3530,
      sentence = [[
"When I tried to change something again, a man showed up here. He told me that there are people who wander between timelines, waiting to correct history."

"He also told me that although Evolvers with time-related abilities were rare, there were still enough of them. What would become of the world if anyone could change the past as they saw fit?"

"But changing something that has already been changed... Is that really 'fixing' it, or is it simply another form of 'change'?"
]],
      music = "30_WarmSnow",
      voice = "est_10112_4.mp3"
    },
    [5] = {
      uid = 948,
      next = 6,
      beijing = 3530,
      sentence = "\"I don't know the answer.\"\n\n\"But no matter what, at the end of all timelines, there was only ever one ending... And it has never changed.\"\n\nVictor took a long time to think. I had seen that face before. He was trying to extract every single piece of useful information from what I said.\n\n—Which was boring.\n\nThere was no point trying to deduce something that had already been proven.\n",
      music = "30_WarmSnow",
      voice = "est_10112_5.mp3"
    },
    [6] = {
      uid = 949,
      next = 7,
      beijing = 3530,
      sentence = [[
"You said it took three years to fix something you altered. Are you sure not a single detail was changed during those three years?"

For about half a second, Victor had me speechless.

"The violin I designed was given a new name at the time. Perhaps one day, some archeologist could dig it up and study it."

It was clear Victor had a lot of expectations for this line of questioning. Yet, I still mercilessly disproved his hypothesis.
]],
      music = "30_WarmSnow",
      voice = "est_10112_6.mp3"
    },
    [7] = {
      uid = 950,
      next = 8,
      beijing = 3530,
      sentence = [[
"But she is different."

"Different from everybody."

"Her fate is entwined with every single timeline, so she is destined to have the only possible ending, together with this world."

"You are different, too."

"And I do feel pity for you. Whether it's the past or the future, you are the only person who can completely manipulate 'time', which means you are meant to carry this enormous responsibility."
]],
      music = "30_WarmSnow",
      voice = "est_10112_7.mp3"
    },
    [8] = {
      uid = 951,
      next = 9,
      beijing = 3530,
      sentence = [[
"...The responsibility that belongs to every member of the Spacetime Bureau."

Victor, who had always remained expressionless, finally frowned.

"What does the Spacetime Bureau have to do with me."

I was about to reply, but he turned and walked away. I realized then that he wasn't asking a question.
]],
      music = "30_WarmSnow",
      voice = "est_10112_8.mp3"
    },
