      uid = 3325,
      next = 3,
      beijing = 2255,
      sentence = "A few days before, Shaw and that young lady came to the shop asking him for a copy of the Millet Gate Academy Codex. Rationally speaking, it was impossible that he'd misremember such a rare and valuable book of engraved tablet rubbings, but he couldn't find it anywhere. If such a thing had only happened once or twice, then perhaps he could chalk it up to old age. But similar situations had occurred multiple times now, so Juan was forced to take it seriously—after all, he was famous on this street as a walking card catalog of sorts. If a book passed through his hands, even if no longer in his possession, then he always knew its whereabouts. Since getting into this business thirty-odd years ago, he could count on one hand how many times he'd misremembered one.\n\nStumped by this, the only thing Juan could do was arrive at the shop a little earlier every day and take an inventory of the books all over again, confirming locations and reshelving, and also keeping a sharp lookout for those books that he hadn't been able to deliver promptly to clients. But the inventory was just half of it. He discovered the number of misplaced books in the shop was greater than he'd imagined, and some books he had absolutely no memory of whatsoever.",
