      sentence = "The afternoon sunlight poured lazily into the room, pooling over the desk in a warm hush. The only noise came from the keyboard—light, rhythmic clacks as words fell into place, character by character.\n\nShaw's fingers drummed against the keys in thought. After a while, he leaned back, exhaling in satisfaction, stretching like a cat settling into a patch of sun. But then, his gaze flickered to the screen, and his expression twisted.\n\n33,479 words. After all that adding, cutting, and revising, the damn word count hadn't changed.\n\nWith a sharp snap, he shut the laptop and reached for the soda can beside him. It was cool to the touch. He took a long swig, letting the icy burn slide down his throat.",
