      beijing = 1761,
      sentence = "Even after meeting with her, something kept gnawing at him, like a tangled emotion he couldn't quite unravel.\n\nShe had stumbled over her words, telling him she wanted to witness history with him. Then, she just looked at him—eyes wide, hopeful, carrying both regret and some strange sense of relief.\n\nWhen he didn't answer right away, she started rambling, spilling her worries. She was scared he was just saying things without meaning them. She was scared he'd leave her behind. The more she thought, the more anxious she became.\n\nBut then, without a word, Shaw reached over and took her hand. And just like that, her restless thoughts dissolved, scattered like dust in the wind.",
