  [82094] = {
    [1] = {
      uid = 3534,
      next = 2,
      beijing = 2220,
      sentence = "Shaw studied the Dragonfly Eye in his palm. The cracks had deepened—splintering across its surface like fractures in glass. He ran a quick calculation, estimating how many times he could still save and reload.\n\nThe answer was grim. This world was reaching its final curtain call.\n\n\"If the whole damn world's about to go up in flames, then what's the point of holding back? It's not like we're gonna leave anything behind. Might as well go out with a bang while we still can!\"\n\nA booming voice spread the tempting words through the crowd like wildfire. Shaw frowned.\n\nHe was standing inside a large shelter complex, constructed by the last remaining governments of the world. High above, the domed ceiling stretched out like a sky trapped in steel. The massive artificial city had been divided into sections as they clung on to whatever time remained.",
      music = "46_Split_in_Black"
    },
    [2] = {
      uid = 3535,
      next = 3,
      beijing = 2220,
      sentence = "The view from where he stood was wide and open—a communal hub where people weaved between makeshift storefronts, gathering whatever supplies they still needed. It wasn't a bad place, but it was a far cry from the life they'd left behind.\n\nThe speaker's voice continued to rise, feeding off the energy of the shifting crowd. Hesitation flickered into intrigue, and intrigue into a burning fanaticism.\n\nAnd then, someone interrupted, \"Who says nothing's gonna be left behind?\"\n\n\"Everything we create, everything we build—it's gonna be seen by the future. If all you care about is indulging yourself, fine, but don't drag the rest of the world down with you!\" The words belonged to a teenager. He was still in his school uniform, but his expression burned with defiance.",
      music = "46_Split_in_Black"
    },
    [3] = {
      uid = 3536,
      next = 4,
      beijing = 2220,
      sentence = "\"Yeah? And what's that worth?\" The speaker sneered, looking down at the kid like he was some naive fool. \"You really think any of that matters? By the time the future rolls around, you and me—we'll both be long gone, buried in places no one even remembers.\"\n\n\"How old are you, huh? What, fifteen? Sixteen? What the hell do you even know about the world? Maybe think twice before you start preaching.\"\n\n\"The world's ending, kid. Can't believe you're still clinging to that school-taught morality crap. I say we make the most of it before everything turns to dust. What's so wrong with that?\"\n\nThe aggression in his stance grew. He jabbed a finger into the boy's shoulder, shoving him back, daring him to break. The boy staggered slightly, but his feet held firm. His face burned red, and his hands clenched into fists at his sides. Then, before the situation could spiral further, another voice stepped in.",
      music = "46_Split_in_Black"
    },
    [4] = {
      uid = 3537,
      next = 5,
      beijing = 2220,
      sentence = "\"Alright, break it off.\" A figure unhurriedly emerged from the audience—an elderly man. He positioned himself beside the boy, looking between the two with a calm, knowing gaze.\n\n\"Sure, the world might be on its last legs. But it hasn't ended yet, has it? You talk like you know what's gonna happen tomorrow. Well, you don't.\" The old man's voice was gentle, but there was no mistaking the weight behind his words. The speaker scoffed, rolling up his sleeves as he avoided the question he had no answers for.\n\n\"The world may be ending, but that does not mean our morals must also crumble. Our lives may end, but the good in our hearts that makes us human must not perish. If we give up our humanity and our morals, then are we not dead already?\" The elderly man pressed his hand upon the teenager's shoulder, his gaze fixed sharply at the preacher.",
      music = "46_Split_in_Black"
    },
    [5] = {
      uid = 3538,
      next = 0,
      beijing = 2220,
      sentence = "The man's face twisted in anger. But before he could lash out, a group of young men stepped forward—positioning themselves between him and the old man like a staunch wall.\n\nAnd then, one by one, more people stepped forward. Quiet, resolute, like mountains standing against the storm, like shields refusing to break.\n\n\"If only all stories unfolded like this.\" Shaw stood at a distance, watching as he recorded this world's every moment.\n\nHe lifted the Dragonfly Eye to his forehead, locking this moment in time. Then, without hesitation, he turned and walked away, down streets that led into the distance.\n\nEven if time rewound again, he'd still refuse to live in a world where he had trod before.",
      music = "46_Split_in_Black"
