      beijing = 1144,
      sentence = "The storm rolled in, thick clouds of dust swallowing the city whole. High-rises disappeared into the shifting haze, as if they had never existed. The streets were nearly empty. The few remaining figures moved quickly, heads low, as if hoping to outrun the inevitable.\n\nShaw strolled through the hollowed-out cityscape, like a lone dot on a canvas of desolation.\n\nScreens flickered overhead, broadcasting the same loop of disaster warnings—volcanic eruptions, tsunamis, endless calamities stacked on top of each other. Destruction had become mundane, and the people left behind had long since stopped resisting. No one raged. No one despaired. They simply accepted it.\n\nAfter seeing each other through their final wishes, he and the girl had parted ways—both with things they needed to do alone.",
